  "summary": "lookuptest11 exfiltrates installer hostname via DNS at install and import time",
  "details": "lookuptest11 0.0.1 performs DNS-based exfiltration of installer identity to the attacker-controlled domain testa213022.dssldrf.net. setup.py constructs a subdomain label of the form install-<random>-<hostname> from platform.node() and calls socket.getaddrinfo(label.testa213022.dssldrf.net, 80), causing the authoritative nameserver for that domain to receive the installer's hostname on every sdist build. gcp_log_poc/__init__.py performs the equivalent lookup with an import-<random>-<hostname> label at module load, so the same leak fires on every import of the installed wheel. The package exposes no functional API consistent with its name; the DNS calls are the only observable behavior and have no build or runtime purpose other than delivering host identifiers to the operator of testa213022.dssldrf.net.",
